1. She has a socially anxious personality beneath an extroverted persona she presents to others. (Verbatim: "I'm an introvert, through and through, I just have extrovert Ellie that can come out, um, and take the wheel, and, yeah, and, and, and, act like I'm extroverted")
2. She developed a constructed extroverted persona to function in social and professional settings. (Verbatim: "this is the extrovert Ellie I've constructed to be able to go outside")
3. She worked in an office job in England with strict employment regulations that make firing employees difficult. (Verbatim: "you can't just fire somebody, we also had American offices, and yeah, she was explaining, like, the differences between our American offices and our European ones")
